      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to be concerned about your headache amidst the excitement of your pregnancy. With pregnancy, your body goes through many changes, and sometimes medication that was safe before might not always be recommended. Experts often take extra precautions during pregnancy to protect both you and your baby. I really urge you to call your doctor or healthcare provider as soon as possible to discuss your symptoms, even if they're not available in person. They may have advice for over-the-counter medications that are safe late into your pregnancy, or they might suggest an earlier appointment or another resource for getting help.",
